From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:54:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 214/342] meson_vdec: the H.264 encoder (HCODEC) as
 /dev/video/meson_venc/0

Written from docs/m48-venc-facts.md (the facts of Amlogic's vendor
driver): power and clock (500 MHz), Amlogic's microcode by IMEM DMA
(the caller gives it: meson_venc_firmware), the reconstruction and
reference frames, and before each command every unit programmed again
(the vendor's full mode). Pictures come from an input area the caller
clones: NV12, NV21, RGB24, or B_RGB32 (the input reader's RGBA mode,
with its byte lanes turning each pixel around). One QP a picture.

On the board: Baseline H.264 that FFmpeg decodes and the hardware
decoder decodes bit for bit as FFmpeg; 1920x1080 in 19.4 ms a picture,
1280x720 in 9.0 ms. GXBB's microcode answers P pictures with IDR_DONE.

The decoder's power code now shares a lock and a counted DOS clock
with the encoder, and sets only its own bits of DOS_GCLK_EN0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
